ZERO.PROOF / evidence of superiority and security

STATUS / 2026-10-07

NOT-PROVEN for the complete language.

The repository now separates:
  PROVEN
  EXHAUSTIVELY-TESTED
  EMPIRICALLY-STRESS-TESTED
  REPRODUCED
  NOT-PROVEN

SECURITY GATE

No "infallible" claim is permitted.

A complete proof requires:
  specification
  formal semantics
  machine-checked safety proofs
  refinement proof from implementation to semantics
  compiler/translator correctness where applicable
  explicit hardware/environment assumptions
  adversarial testing
  independent reproduction

CURRENT MACHINE-CHECKED MODEL

proof/ZeroSafety.v defines and proves:
  - secret preservation
  - public-step independence from secret state
  - budget consumption
  - budget precondition

These are proofs of the abstract model only.

CURRENT TEST CAMPAIGN

ZERO.BILLION-TESTS defines 256 shards x 2^24 cases = 2^32 cases.
browser-core/zero_campaign.c is deterministic and reproducible from case_id.
A local validation of the campaign logic executed 1,000,000 cases successfully.

The 2^32 campaign is configured in GitHub Actions.
It must not be reported as executed until every shard has a PASS artifact.

KNOWN BLOCKERS

B1
  The current C implementation is not formally connected to proof/ZeroSafety.v.
  Required: refinement/correctness proof.

B2
  FIXED in the native prototype: event state is now owned by ZeroCore and
  zero_last_event() requires the owning core instance. The remaining obligation
  is to prove the isolation property and add an adversarial two-instance test.

B3
  ZERO.EXECUTION says a transition is accepted only when it changes the
  observable field, while some C paths can return without emitting a new event.
  Required: reconcile the executable semantics and the language specification.

B4
  The current proof model does not yet cover memory safety, device authority,
  network authority, GPU/display authority, parser correctness, side channels,
  accessibility preservation, recovery, or hostile external effects.
  Required: additional formal models and refinement proofs.

B5
  The experimental Rust discovery engine, C browser prototype and Rocq model
  remain separate evidence domains. Required: a shared semantic contract and
  refinement chain.

SUPERSET

  docs/PROPERTY-SUPERSET.md defines P01-P35, extending I0-I10 with authority,
  mediation, provenance, concurrency, device effects, compiler preservation,
  accessibility, self-extension containment, recovery and proof composition.

PROMOTION RULE

A property is CORE only when:
  1. specified;
  2. formally proved for the model;
  3. connected to implementation by refinement proof;
  4. adversarially tested;
  5. independently reproduced.

A benchmark can never upgrade NOT-PROVEN to PROVEN.
